  {
   "id": "gceal-maths-partial-fractions",
   "title": "Partial fractions and their integration",
   "minutes": 25,
   "programRef": "Cameroon GCE Board — Advanced Level Mathematics, Pure Mathematics (Upper Sixth part; to be checked against the official syllabus)",
   "status": "draft",
   "author": "CastBridge (AI draft)",
   "source": "Original writing following the Cameroonian curriculum; to be reviewed by a teacher",
   "objectives": [
    "Split a rational function into partial fractions",
    "Handle improper fractions",
    "Integrate the results"
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "exercises": [
    "gceal-maths-integration-e13",
    "gceal-maths-integration-e14",
    "gceal-maths-integration-e15",
    "gceal-maths-integration-e16",
    "gceal-maths-integration-e17",
    "gceal-maths-integration-e18"
   ],
   "selfCheck": [
    "gceal-maths-partial-fractions-q1",
    "gceal-maths-partial-fractions-q2",
    "gceal-maths-partial-fractions-q3",
    "gceal-maths-partial-fractions-q4",
    "gceal-maths-partial-fractions-q5"
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
    "Repeated-factor and quadratic-factor cases are described but only distinct linear factors are exercised.",
    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Partial fractions",
     "md": "For distinct linear factors: $\\frac{px+q}{(x-a)(x-b)}=\\frac{A}{x-a}+\\frac{B}{x-b}$. Multiply by the denominator and substitute $x=a$ (to get $A$) and $x=b$ (to get $B$) - the cover-up method. For a repeated factor use $\\frac{A}{x-a}+\\frac{B}{(x-a)^2}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Improper fractions",
     "md": "If the degree of the numerator is at least that of the denominator, divide first. Example: $\\frac{x^2}{x^2-1}=1+\\frac{1}{x^2-1}$, and then split $\\frac{1}{(x-1)(x+1)}=\\frac{1/2}{x-1}-\\frac{1/2}{x+1}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "propriete",
     "title": "Integrating",
     "md": "$\\int\\frac{A}{x-a}dx=A\\ln|x-a|+C$. After integrating, combine logs with $\\ln p+\\ln q=\\ln pq$ and $\\ln p-\\ln q=\\ln\\frac pq$ to give an exact answer."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "Do not forget to check your constants (substitute another value of $x$). A fraction that is improper must be divided first. $\\int\\frac{1}{x-a}dx$ is a logarithm, not $-\\frac{1}{(x-a)^2}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Express $\\frac{5x+1}{(x-1)(x+2)}$ in partial fractions.",
     "steps": [
      "Write $5x+1=A(x+2)+B(x-1)$.",
      "$x=1$: $6=3A$, $A=2$. $x=-2$: $-9=-3B$, $B=3$.",
      "Check at $x=0$: LHS $=-\\frac{1}{2}$; RHS $=-2+\\frac{3}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}$."
     ],
     "answer": "$\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{3}{x+2}$",
     "figure": {
      "kind": "plot",
      "xmin": 1.2,
      "xmax": 6,
      "ymin": -2,
      "ymax": 12,
      "grid": 1,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 260,
      "curves": [
       {
        "expr": "(5x+1)/((x-1)(x+2))",
        "color": "blue"
       }
      ],
      "points": [],
      "segments": [],
      "xlabel": "x"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Evaluate $\\int_2^3\\frac{5x+1}{(x-1)(x+2)}dx$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\int\\left(\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{3}{x+2}\\right)dx=2\\ln|x-1|+3\\ln|x+2|$.",
      "$[\\,]_2^3=(2\\ln2+3\\ln5)-(2\\ln1+3\\ln4)=2\\ln2+3\\ln\\frac{5}{4}$."
     ],
     "answer": "$2\\ln2+3\\ln\\frac{5}{4}\\approx2.056$"
    }
   ],
